[Music]  the season one finale of 1883 the  paramount plus prequel series to  paramount's yellowstone might just be  the most heartbreaking episode in the  entire yellowstone franchise first and  foremost there are two major character  deaths in the finale both of whom  successfully reached the end of their  respective journeys before passing the  first is elsa dutton who after being  gravely wounded by an arrow makes her  father james promise that she can pick  the spot where she will die she ends up  choosing a small tree in the gorgeous  paradise valley and dies peacefully in  her father's arms the scene is  gut-wrenching and tragic though the  episode's second major death is by far  the more brutal of the two in a time  skip forward we watch as shae brennan  finally completes his journey to the  west coast and sits on a beach in oregon  to watch the waves crash against the  shore it was revealed earlier in the  series that shea's only reason for  making the journey west was because of a  promise he made to his wife helen who  desperately wanted to see the ocean just  look at that helen  beautiful  helen died prior to the series start so  shea took it upon himself to let her see  the ocean through his eyes shea's  promise is finally fulfilled and after  staring at the waves for a while he  kills himself so that he can finally be  with his wife once more  given how well audiences had gotten to  know shay throughout 1883 season 1 his  death is undeniably sad although there  is a silver lining that makes the scene  a bit less heartbreaking the unexpected  appearance of a hummingbird on the beach  which flits around for a moment looking  right at him as if it's trying to get  his attention it doesn't stay long  though and when it leaves a smile widens  across jay's face who has finally found  peace in his final moments the 1883  reddit community naturally began  speculating on what this scene and the  bird itself means a prevalent theory is  that the hummingbird symbolizes someone  visiting shae from beyond the grave  specifically his late wife helen it  could be that the hummingbird is indeed  shay's wife who comes to see him at the  end of their long journey to oregon  after all seeing what was supposed to be  their adventure through to the end was  shay's driving purpose all along so it  makes thematic sense still other fans  seem to believe that it's actually an  entirely different deceased character  one reddit user wrote it was elsa the  symbolism of the hummingbird is the  epitome of her remember her talking  about birds in her final moment other  users referenced elsa's conversation  with shea earlier in the episode which  seems to foreshadow his meeting with the  bird as one poster wrote elsa did tell  him to save a spot for her at the beach  if she didn't survive it seems entirely  possible that the hummingbird is meant  to symbolize elsa coming back to visit  shea just like she said she would come  at you on the beach  i'll save your spot then there's the  third camp which includes people who  just found the whole scene absolutely  tear-jerking and didn't dwell much on  the symbolism at all calling the scene  sad but also beautiful one person posted  shea on the beach with the hummingbird  really got me i know his body and soul  were tired and he was ready to be with  his wife and daughter other users wrote  that they loved shay and elsa's  connection throughout the first season  of the series all the way up to the  bittersweet end regardless of who the  hummingbird really is its appearance is  undeniably heartwarming and makes an  incredibly emotional scene even more  powerful shea brennan's life was  dominated by war loss and sadness which  compounded to create the gruff  no-nonsense attitude that became his  trademark at least when he sat on that  beach looked on at the vastness of the  ocean and had the chance to breathe just  a little easier he didn't have to do so  alone check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite movies and tv shows  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

